  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre PEZA-registered enterprises subject to corporate income tax under Philippine law?\n\n### Short Answer\nYes, PEZA-registered enterprises are subject to corporate income tax, but they may benefit from preferential tax rates and incentives under specific conditions.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provision is Section 27 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which outlines the rates of income tax on domestic corporations. Specifically, it states that a corporate income tax rate of twenty-five percent (25%) is imposed on the taxable income derived from all sources within and without the Philippines by every corporation.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nPEZA-registered enterprises should assess their eligibility for the 5% tax rate on gross income, which is significantly lower than the standard corporate income tax rate. It is crucial for these enterprises to maintain compliance with PEZA regulations and ensure proper documentation to avail of these tax incentives. Additionally, they should be aware of the implications of their income sources, as income derived from outside the economic zones may be subject to different tax treatments.",
